-- ============================================================================
-- FC7 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Produced Water Treatment, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE THREE DEVICES WHOSE CUT DOES NOT COME FROM GRAVITY
-- ALONE. The grade efficiency curve and the removal as an integral over the
-- distribution; the hydrocyclone on stated geometry, a field, a travel from the
-- half-area radius to the oil core and a residence time; the operating
-- envelope, where the field stops rising at 1.3 times design, the inlet shear
-- penalty starts, and the module refuses past twice design and names the bank
-- the flow wants; flotation as attachment kinetics; the media bed as depth
-- filtration read backwards; and the KOKORI train through all three.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. A liner bank is sized in LINERS, and the
-- sweep a designer saving money reads, taking liners out, improves and then
-- TURNS OVER. A model whose answer improves without limit as an input is pushed
-- has no limit in it.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The bubble rise velocity is on every
-- flotation return and does not reach the cut size at all: the rate carries
-- the gas flux over the cube of the bubble diameter. The IZOMBE capstone grades
-- the rise velocity and the holdup it sets, and not the flotation cut, which is
-- the one answer that reads the calibration.
--
-- HELD FOR LITERATURE, and neutralised by construction on the capstone: the
-- attachment efficiency is read by no graded field (the capstone generator
-- moves it tenfold and asserts the graded rise and holdup do not change by a
-- single bit), and the bed is packed at the module's own reference grain, where
-- the held inverse-cube exponent multiplies by exactly one.
-- ============================================================================

